  "_comment": "NORMATIVE. The single definition of how the nineteen lifecycle statuses project onto what each surface shows. The SERVER computes every column here and returns it; no client may recompute any of them. Both clients carry a test that asserts their own implementation matches this file exactly, so a drift is a failed build rather than a wrong answer shown to an applicant.",
  "contractVersion": "0.1.0",
  "source": "Derived from the eBPCO Web Admin's status.model.ts (LIFECYCLE_TO_MOBILE_LABEL, coarseStatus) via tools/extract_admin_vocabulary.py, plus the two columns decided in TAB 01.",
  "columns": {
    "applicantStatus": "One of the seven applicant-visible states. Wire field `applicantStatus`.",
    "coarseStatus": "The three-value projection the admin's board columns render. Not transmitted; derived identically by both tiers.",
    "requiresApplicantAction": "Whether the LGU is waiting on the applicant. Deliberately independent of applicantStatus: Revision Required and Assessed both project onto passive headlines ('Under Review', 'Payment Verification') that give the applicant no hint they are the one holding the application up. Wire field `requiresApplicantAction`.",
    "terminal": "No further processing will happen. Suppresses any pledge countdown.",
    "pledgeApplies": "Whether an RA 11032 countdown is meaningful — the LGU still owes an act. False for Draft (not yet filed) and every terminal state."
  },
